    "forensics": "The losing cluster was primarily driven by transaction fee drag turning marginally profitable or flat trades (e.g., ICICIBANK and afternoon TATASTEEL setups) into net losses upon breakeven stops or EOD square-offs. Furthermore, several cyclical equities (NTPC, TATASTEEL) hit stop-losses right at the 0.68% boundary due to normal intraday volatility noise during mid-day and pre-lunch consolidations. Overly ambitious profit targets (1.15%) and late breakeven triggers (1.1R) caused winning positions to revert before profits could be locked in.",
    "learning": "In low-capital NSE cash equity trading, transaction costs (STT, brokerage, exchange charges) create a severe asymmetric hurdle where breakeven exits and stagnant afternoon entries bleed capital; strategies must demand higher institutional volume conviction on sweeps while pulling in profit targets and breakeven triggers to capture core momentum bursts before mean reversion sets in.",
